					<h1 class="title" title="Gandhinagar - a perfect holiday destination">Gandhinagar - a perfect holiday destination</h1>
<div class="entry-content">

<h3>History and location </h3>
<p>Located in the <b>western part of India, Gandhinagar</b> is the <b>capital city of Gujarat</b>. It is situated 
on the banks of <b>river Sabarmati</b>. It is also known as the <b>greenest capital in India</b> and with the 
beautiful city <b>Ahmedabad</b> close by, it has emerged as a tourist spot too. People who come to visit Ahmedabad 
make it a must to visit Gandhinagar too. It is just 30 km. away from Ahmedabad. It is believed to have n built by 
Sultan Ahmed Shah who is also said to construct the city of Ahmedabad. </p>


<h3>Places to see</h3>

<p>The most <b>popular place in Gandhinagar</b> is the <b>Akshardham temple</b>. It is a very splendid work of 
art with beautiful carvings by <b>pink stones</b>. All around the temple are beautiful lush green gardens and 
fresh water fountains. They also organize laser shows in the evening to which also attracts many tourists. Around 
18 km. south of Gandhinagar, is another place of attraction known as the <b>Adlaj Ni Vav</b> which was built by 
Rani Rudrabai in the 15 century. The Vav, so called in Gujarat is the step well which is intricately carved with 
beautiful floral designs. </p>


<p>An amusement park or the <b>Children’s park in sector 28</b> is also a tourist attraction providing many rides, 
boating facilities and other kinds of amusement to the kids as well as the grown ups. A toy train is also a nice 
adventure here.  The <b>Deer park</b> or the <b>Indroda Park</b> is a perfect place for those seeking peace and 
solace from the regular hustle bustle of the city.  There is also a <b>Dinosaurs Park</b> here with various 
statues of dinosaurs worth seeing. A python cage, an aquarium and the snake park are other attractions in the 
Deer park. A beautiful garden known as the <b>Sarita Garden</b> situated on the banks of <b>River Sabarmati</b> 
is a nice picnic spot .the craftsmen village at Pethapur is another good place to know the 
<b>cultural heritage of Gujarat</b>.  An excellent piece of work is the the domed building, the Capital Complex 
<b>VitthalBhai Patel Bhavan</b>. Some tourists also make a visit to the <b>Gujarat Law University</b>.</p> 

<p>A botanical garden with is an amalgation of botanical species along with the zodiac signs is the Punit Van in 
sector 19 of Gandhinagar. Am amphitheatre is also a major attraction here. Some close by attractions is also the 
<b>golden beaches of Daman and Diu</b> not very far from here. </p>



